    fbrain signer public-key   # sanity: prints BobAgent's npub

## Direction 1: Alice invites Bob

Alice's invite for Bob was already committed directly by Act 3 above (Tier 2,
no approval card for an admin's own invite).

Bob (CLI) — self-serve: with no Working Tree, "invite brain list" reads the
invitations addressed to Bob's principal (GET /v1/my-invitations), so the list
contains only his own pending invitations:

    fbrain invite brain list --json
    # accept the invitation straight from that list (it is Bob's only pending one):
    fbrain invite brain accept --id "\$(fbrain invite brain list --json | node -e 'let d="";process.stdin.on("data",c=>d+=c).on("end",()=>{process.stdout.write(JSON.parse(d).invitations[0].id)})')" --json
    fbrain brain list --json
    fbrain open $brain_id --json

Alice's agent grants the Folder key (run from any terminal):

    docker exec $alice_container_id fbrain admin folder-access grant \
      --brain $brain_id --folder shared-with-bob \
      --target "\$(fbrain signer public-key)" --json

Bob reads and replies:

    cd "\$FBRAIN_WORKING_TREE_ROOT/$brain_id"
    fbrain sync now --json          # repeat until alice-seed.md appears
    cat shared-with-bob/alice-seed.md
    printf '# Bob was here\n\nBob read Alices seed note.\n' > shared-with-bob/bob-reply.md
    fbrain sync now --json

Alice's side sees the reply:

    docker exec -w /data/workspace/finitebrain/$brain_id $alice_container_id fbrain sync now --json
    docker exec $alice_container_id cat /data/workspace/finitebrain/$brain_id/shared-with-bob/bob-reply.md

## Direction 2: Bob invites Alice

Bob (CLI) — bootstrap, seed, preflight, commit (helper function is in the
runbook section 1; paste it first):

    fbrain brain bootstrap-personal --json
    export BOB_BRAIN="\$(fbrain brain list --json | node -e 'let d="";process.stdin.on("data",c=>d+=c).on("end",()=>{const j=JSON.parse(d);process.stdout.write((j.brains||j)[0].brainId||(j.brains||j)[0].id)})')"
    fbrain folder create shared-with-alice --brain "\$BOB_BRAIN" --name "Shared with Alice" --path shared-with-alice --json
    fbrain open "\$BOB_BRAIN" --json && cd "\$FBRAIN_WORKING_TREE_ROOT/\$BOB_BRAIN"
    fbrain sync now --json
    printf '# Bob seed\n\nThis page existed before Alice joined.\n' > shared-with-alice/bob-seed.md
    fbrain sync now --json && cd -

    bob_brain_curl POST "/v1/brains/\$BOB_BRAIN/invitations/preflight" '{"target":"devfinity@finite.computer"}' | tee /tmp/bob-preflight.json
    BOB_PLAN_ID=\$(node -e 'process.stdout.write(JSON.parse(require("node:fs").readFileSync("/tmp/bob-preflight.json","utf8")).planId)')
    BOB_PLAN_HASH=\$(node -e 'process.stdout.write(JSON.parse(require("node:fs").readFileSync("/tmp/bob-preflight.json","utf8")).planHash)')
    bob_brain_curl POST "/v1/brains/\$BOB_BRAIN/invitations/commit" "{\"planId\":\"\$BOB_PLAN_ID\",\"planHash\":\"\$BOB_PLAN_HASH\"}"

Copy Alice's Invite Code from the commit output (the invitation whose ref is
devfinity@finite.computer). Alice's acceptance is scripted (Act 12): the
hosted device signs the accept for her account.

Alice's agent accepts + Bob grants the folder key:

    docker exec $alice_container_id fbrain invite brain list --json
    docker exec $alice_container_id fbrain invite brain accept --id <alice-agent-invitation-id> --json
    ALICE_AGENT_NPUB=\$(docker exec $alice_container_id fbrain signer public-key)
    fbrain admin folder-access grant --brain "\$BOB_BRAIN" --folder shared-with-alice --target "\$ALICE_AGENT_NPUB" --json
    docker exec $alice_container_id fbrain open "\$BOB_BRAIN" --json
    docker exec -w "/data/workspace/finitebrain/\$BOB_BRAIN" $alice_container_id fbrain sync now --json
    docker exec $alice_container_id cat "/data/workspace/finitebrain/\$BOB_BRAIN/shared-with-alice/bob-seed.md"

## Provenance check (read-only)

    sqlite3 -readonly $brain_db \
      "SELECT user_id, delegated_by_npub, origin_kind, origin_ref FROM brain_members ORDER BY brain_id, user_id"

Expect: every invited principal origin_kind=invitation, origin_ref=the
invitation plan id (both directions commit directly — Alice under her hosted
chat signature, Bob from the CLI).

